# CIU-generated files (do not commit). Sample rules to copy into a project's
# .gitignore. Note: a hand-written docker-compose.yml (for the plain
# `docker compose` / `ciu --shipped` path) is committed and NOT listed here.
#
# NOT listed below, and must NOT be gitignored: `ciu.global.toml.j2` and
# `**/ciu.toml.j2` (SPEC S3.1a, CIU-8) -- committed, hand-authored SPARSE
# OVERRIDE templates. CIU never auto-creates either one; they belong in git
# next to the *.defaults.toml.j2 files they override. Only the RENDERED
# ciu.global.toml / ciu.toml (below) are gitignored. CIU's own `.gitignore`
# in this repo documents the identical distinction with the identical
# reasoning -- see it for the worked example. (CIU-61 found this sample file
# had drifted and wrongly listed both templates as ignored; corrected here.)

# machine identity layer (S2) -- regenerated by `ciu env generate`
ciu.env

# managed worktree identity/lifecycle record (S16)
ciu.worktree-instance.json

# CIU machine-owned artifact directory (S1.6/S1.7)
**/.ciu/

# rendered global config -- track the .j2 source (ciu.global.toml.j2, NOT
# gitignored, see the callout above), not this rendered output
ciu.global.toml

# per-checkout sparse global override (S3.1b) -- gitignored (unlike the
# committed ciu.global.toml.j2 above); hand-authored and machine-specific.
# Renamed from ciu.global.worktree.toml.j2 by ciu-P47 (hard cutover: the old
# name is not read, and `ciu migration-check` reports a leftover copy).
ciu.global.instance.toml.j2

# CIU-owned generated identity facts (S3.1b) -- plain TOML, never a template,
# rewritten in full by every `ciu env generate`. Carries
# [ciu.instance.generated], the SOLE instance-identity source since
# CIU-75/7.7.0; split out of the overlay above by ciu-P47.
ciu.instance.generated.toml

# rendered per-stack config -- track the ciu.toml.j2 source (NOT gitignored,
# see the callout above), not this rendered output
**/ciu.toml

# CIU's own rendered compose output for .j2 templates (S8.1)
**/ciu.compose.yml
